=== APPROACH ===
- The repository's WinUI app is code-first C# (no .xaml page files); every feature surface lives under
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/<Name>/ as <Name>.Model.cs (pure, Microsoft.UI-free projection,
  unit-tested headlessly), <Name>.Source.cs (the generated-client feed), <Name>.ViewModel.cs
  (INotifyPropertyChanged + IDisposable state holder) and <Name>.cs (the Fluent view), exactly as the sibling W7
  FeatureFlagsPage / ActiveSessionsPage / DLQInspectorPage do. The generated prompt's idealized
  "RbacMatrixPage.xaml + RbacMatrixPageViewModel.cs under TeslaSync/Features/Admin" is mapped onto these real
  conventions. The web page is unrouted in App.tsx, so the surface is registered Hidden in RouteTable.cs
  (Hidden("RbacMatrix","admin/rbac",RouteGroup.AdminDevTools)) — deep-linkable / route-coverage visible without
  inventing a nav entry the web does not have — and wired to the W4 ShellPageFactory by route name "RbacMatrix"
  (ShellWindow.xaml.cs).
- The page reproduces every web region with Fluent components + design tokens (ADR-005): the page header
  (PageTitle + Subhead), GlassPanel 1 = the AUTH_MODE_OPEN forward-auth notice (TsGlassPanel + Heading + HelperText),
  GlassPanel 2 = the summary (the MyRoles + Effective TsBadge pills, the optional groups-header Caption and the
  Edit / Save / Cancel TsButtons), GlassPanel 3 = the matrix (a role × permission Grid with read-only check/dash
  cells or, in edit mode, TsCheckbox toggles, rebuilt structurally on snapshot/edit change so an in-edit toggle never
  tears down the check boxes). The loading / empty / error branches render through the shared feedback surfaces
  (TsSpinner / TsEmptyState / TsAlertBanner + Retry). Never a blank region (ADR-006).
- Edit flow (web handleEnterEdit / handleToggle / handleCancelEdit / handleSave): EnterEdit reseeds a mutable draft
  from the snapshot; Toggle mutates one draft cell; DirtyCount = RbacMatrix.DiffMatrices(snapshot.Matrix, draft).Count
  drives the "Save (n)" label + the enabled state; SaveAsync PUTs only the changed cells and, on success, exits edit
  and re-runs the read (web invalidates the ['admin','rbac','matrix'] query); a save failure keeps the matrix in edit
  mode and records submitError. The PUT is RequireSudo-gated upstream; the reauth challenge fires transparently.
- Data binding (ADR-004): the manifest data sources are the web hooks useRbacMatrix / useUpsertRbacCells and the pure
  helpers diffMatrices / isRbacOpenMode (kept at their web names: RbacMatrix.DiffMatrices / RbacMatrix.IsRbacOpenMode).
  The view-model reads/writes through two injected ports (IRbacMatrixFeed / IRbacWriteService, RbacMatrixPage.Model.cs);
  the default OpenModeRbacMatrixFeed/NoopRbacWriteService resolve the truthful local-state open-auth notice (the
  sibling host-injection precedent), and the generated-client-backed RbacMatrixClientFeed / RbacUpsertClientService
  (RbacMatrixPage.Source.cs) bind the generated OpenAPI contract client operations get_api_v1_admin_rbac_matrix /
  put_api_v1_admin_rbac_matrix, asserted against the generated endpoint table + the FakeApiClient in tests. No HTTP
  touches the view. A 501 AUTH_MODE_OPEN (or an explicit { mode: "open" } body) maps to the open-auth notice exactly
  as the web hook treats it; any other non-success surfaces as ApiException → the error branch. The PUT body posts
  { cells: [{ role_id, permission_id, allowed }] } in the snake_case wire shape (never the camelCase record names).
- The web page has no charts and no map (manifest charts=0, maps=0) — none added.
- SI units N/A (this admin surface bears no unit fields — role ids, permission ids/names/categories and allow/deny
  booleans only); nothing is stored or computed in non-SI.
- All 23 i18n keys already exist verbatim (web key names) in Strings/{en,he,ar}/Resources.resw under the
  translation.rbac.* prefix; the surface resolves them through the ILocalizer facade with the web English defaults as
  fallbacks. Parameterized values (actions.save, cell.toggle, effective.count, myRoles.label, groupsHeader.label) are
  stored with the catalog's positional {0}/{1} markers and interpolated via RbacMatrixRegistration.

